      "writtenOn": "2023-04-05T14:29:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since these are always tried together, would it make sense to just extend the existing `parseRGBColorToken` to parse an optional alpha?\n\nE.g. I think you could add this right before `return true` for equivalent behavior:\n\n    // optional alpha\n    int32_t a;\n    if (this-\u003eparseSepToken() \u0026\u0026\n        this-\u003eparseColorComponentScalarToken(\u0026a)) {\n        *c \u003d SkColorSetA(*c, static_cast\u003cuint8_t\u003e(a));\n    }\n\nThen you can keep `parseColorComponentToken` unchanged and just need to add `parseColorComponentScalarToken`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 379,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 380,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "13dacddcfd71b48e499822f916672c78d505517d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a309b10_6a5b72c7",
        "filename": "modules/svg/src/SkSVGAttributeParser.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 380,
      "author": {
        "id": 19829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-26T09:11:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem with doing it this way is that we still need to handle the `this-\u003eparseParenthesized(\"rgba\"...)` that happens before and reusing the code like this might lead us to have a hairy solution to handle the extra \"a\" before the parenthesis.\nI think also compartmentalizing component token into parseColorComponentIntegralToken and parseColorComponentFractionalToken might improve legibility.",
